%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recursiveDefinitionsRequest%27%2C%20definitionSource%2C%20%27recursive-formal-concept-definitions%27%2C%20%27formal-concept-definitions%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-FORMAL-CONCEPT-DEFINITIONS%27%2C%20%27deep%20formal%20definition%20of%20every%20concept%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20concept%20has%20a%20recursively%20inspectable%20formal%20definition%20represented%20as%20links%2C%20with%20explicit%20axioms%2C%20operations%2C%20bindings%20and%20declared%20foundational%20primitives.%20An%20English%20description%20or%20opaque%20semantic%20signature%20is%20insufficient%20as%20its%20formal%20definition.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27everyConceptFormallyDefined%27%2C%20%27definitionsAreInspectableLinks%27%2C%20%27foundationalPrimitivesExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-FORMAL-CONCEPT-REFERENCES%27%2C%20%27mutual%20references%20between%20formal%20concept%20definitions%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Concept%20definitions%20can%20use%20other%20concepts%20recursively%20while%20retaining%20stable%20identities%2C%20qualified%20references%20and%20the%20selected%20foundation.%20Shared%20and%20cyclic%20references%20serialize%20and%20reload%20without%20flattening%20definitions%20or%20discarding%20their%20assumptions.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27recursiveConceptReferencesPreserved%27%2C%20%27sharedAndCyclicDefinitionsReloaded%27%2C%20%27definitionAssumptionsPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-FORMAL-CONCEPT-MEANING-COMPARISON%27%2C%20%27formal%20definitions%20as%20evidence%20of%20equal%20concept%20meaning%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Meaning%20comparison%20uses%20the%20complete%20recursive%20formal%20definitions%20and%20checked%20obligations%20under%20their%20explicit%20foundations.%20Equal%20names%2C%20source%20text%2C%20labels%20or%20declared%20meaning%20signatures%20alone%20cannot%20certify%20semantic%20equivalence%3B%20unresolved%20obligations%20preserve%20separate%20concepts.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27formalDefinitionsCompared%27%2C%20%27semanticObligationsChecked%27%2C%20%27unprovedMeaningEquivalenceRejected%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recursiveDefinitionsRequest%27%2C%20definitionSource%2C%20%27ontology-and-taxonomy-entry-points%27%2C%20%27ontology-and-taxonomy%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-LIBRARY-ENTRYPOINT%27%2C%20%27separate%20ontology%20library%20entry%20point%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20expose%20a%20separate%20ontology%20entry%20point%20for%20concepts%2C%20relationships%20and%20formal%20axioms%20in%20the%20global%20space%2C%20including%20concepts%20unused%20by%20any%20language%20grammar.%20Their%20definitions%20and%20links%20remain%20available%20without%20caller%20grammar%20registration.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27ontologyEntryPointAvailable%27%2C%20%27grammarUnusedConceptsAvailable%27%2C%20%27ontologyDefinitionsAndRelationsInspectable%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TAXONOMY-LIBRARY-ENTRYPOINT%27%2C%20%27separate%20taxonomy%20library%20entry%20point%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20expose%20a%20separate%20taxonomy%20entry%20point%20for%20classification%20and%20explicitly%20declared%20subsumption%20links%20over%20the%20global%20concept%20space%2C%20including%20concepts%20unused%20by%20grammars.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27taxonomyEntryPointAvailable%27%2C%20%27classificationAndSubsumptionInspectable%27%2C%20%27grammarUnusedTaxonomyConceptsAvailable%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-TAXONOMY-MEMBERSHIP%27%2C%20%27concept%20membership%20in%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%20or%20both%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20concept%20can%20occur%20in%20the%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%20or%20both%20through%20the%20same%20global%20identity.%20Grammar%20reachability%20never%20removes%20a%20concept%2C%20and%20both%20entry%20points%20retain%20its%20recursive%20formal%20definition%20and%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27sharedOntologyTaxonomyIdentity%27%2C%20%27membershipIndependentOfGrammarReachability%27%2C%20%27definitionsAndProvenanceRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-TAXONOMY-RELATION-DISTINCTION%27%2C%20%27distinction%20between%20general%20relations%20and%20classification%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20ontology%20represents%20concepts%2C%20relationships%20and%20formal%20axioms%3B%20the%20taxonomy%20represents%20classification%20or%20declared%20subsumption.%20An%20arbitrary%20associative%20relation%20does%20not%20become%20a%20classification%20edge%2C%20and%20the%20chosen%20hierarchy%20semantics%20remain%20explicit%20links.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27ontologyAndTaxonomyRolesDistinct%27%2C%20%27arbitraryRelationsDoNotImplyClassification%27%2C%20%27hierarchySemanticsExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20ontology%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27An%20ontology%20can%20have%20several%20independently%20selectable%20roots%2C%20each%20represented%20as%20an%20explicit%20link%20in%20the%20global%20space.%20A%20root%20may%20also%20be%20a%20type%20only%20when%20its%20model%20declares%20that%20role%3B%20root%20selection%20and%20traversal%20retain%20identity%20and%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleOntologyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TAXONOMY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20taxonomy%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20taxonomy%20can%20have%20several%20explicitly%20represented%20root%20links%20and%20multiple%20classification%20entry%20points.%20A%20root%20type%20role%20is%20declared%20by%20the%20selected%20model%20rather%20than%20inferred%20from%20being%20a%20root%2C%20and%20classification%20traversal%20preserves%20its%20declared%20semantics.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleTaxonomyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27linksFoundationRequest%27%2C%20linksSource%2C%20%27links-as-fundamental-entities-and-relationships%27%2C%20%27links-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-UNIVERSAL-REPRESENTATION%27%2C%20%27links%20as%20the%20fundamental%20representation%20of%20concepts%2C%20entities%20and%20relationships%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20represented%20concept%2C%20entity%2C%20relationship%2C%20root%20and%20formal%20definition%20is%20fundamentally%20a%20link%20or%20composition%20of%20links%20in%20the%20same%20network.%20Independent%20host%20objects%20or%20hidden%20side%20tables%20cannot%20substitute%20for%20the%20common%20representation.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27conceptsEntitiesRelationshipsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27rootsAndDefinitionsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27noHiddenEntityRepresentation%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-SELF-LOOP-VERTEX%27%2C%20%27vertex%20represented%20by%20a%20self-referencing%20link%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20selected%20links%20model%20can%20represent%20a%20vertex%20as%20a%20link%20whose%20beginning%20and%20end%20reference%20that%20same%20link.%20Its%20identity%2C%20self-reference%20and%20selected%20model%20are%20explicit%20and%20survive%20serialization%20and%20reload.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27selfLoopVertexRepresentable%27%2C%20%27selfReferencingEndpointsPreserved%27%2C%20%27vertexModelAndIdentityRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-MULTIPLE-ROLES%27%2C%20%27one%20link%20as%20relationship%2C%20concept%20and%20entity%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20same%20link%20can%20carry%20relationship%2C%20concept%20and%20entity%20roles%20without%20replacing%20its%20identity%20with%20disconnected%20host%20representations.%20Role%20declarations%20and%20multiple%20root%20selections%20remain%20inspectable%20links.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27linkIdentitySharedAcrossRoles%27%2C%20%27rolesAreExplicitLinks%27%2C%20%27multipleRootRolesPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-RECURSIVE-COMPOSITION%27%2C%20%27recursive%20compositional%20links%20across%20representation%20levels%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Links%20can%20reference%20and%20compose%20other%20links%20recursively%20across%20representation%20levels%2C%20preserving%20the%20reusable%20structural%20motif%2C%20shared%20references%20and%20explicit%20cycles.%20This%20compositional%20model%20does%20not%20itself%20establish%20a%20mathematical%20fractal%20dimension%20or%20eliminate%20logical%20paradoxes.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27recursiveLinkCompositionPreserved%27%2C%20%27sharedMotifAndCyclesExplicit%27%2C%20%27noUnprovedConsistencyInference%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-OPTIONAL-TYPE-ROOT%27%2C%20%27declared%20type%20roots%20without%20a%20universal%20self-typing%20axiom%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20model%20may%20declare%20a%20root%20link%20to%20be%20a%20type.%20The%20representation%20does%20not%20infer%20a%20universal%20Type%3AType%20axiom%20or%20a%20universal%20proof%20logic%20from%20links%2C%20self-loops%2C%20recursion%20or%20root%20membership%3B%20foundation%20premises%20remain%20explicit%20and%20selectable.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27rootTypeRolesDeclared%27%2C%20%27noImplicitUniversalSelfTyping%27%2C%20%27selectedFoundationPremisesPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27linksFoundationRequest%27%2C%20linksSource%2C%20%27links-as-fundamental-entities-and-relationships%27%2C%20%27links-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-PHYSICAL-ANALOGY%27%2C%20%27recorded%20wave%20and%20fractal%20motivation%20with%20an%20explicit%20epistemic%20boundary%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20user%20wave%2C%20particle%20and%20fractal%20analogy%20is%20preserved%20verbatim%20as%20motivation%20and%20a%20hypothesis.%20Documentation%20and%20formal%20models%20do%20not%20report%20those%20physical%20propositions%2C%20universal%20self-similarity%20or%20freedom%20from%20contradictions%20as%20established%20facts%20or%20consistency%20proofs.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27physicalAnalogyCapturedVerbatim%27%2C%20%27physicalPropositionsMarkedAsHypotheses%27%2C%20%27noAnalogyPresentedAsConsistencyProof%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recordConversationRequest%27%2C%20recordingSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27conversation-contract%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-CONVERSATION-VERBATIM-REGISTER%27%2C%20%27immutable%20hashed%20capture%20of%20every%20requirement-bearing%20conversation%20message%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20requirement-bearing%20conversation%20message%20is%20captured%20verbatim%20with%20its%20content%20hash%20and%20explicit%20capture%20provenance%2C%20registered%20as%20a%20source%20and%20linked%20to%20atomic%20obligations.%20New%20messages%20append%20captures%20rather%20than%20overwriting%20earlier%20requests.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27conversationMessagesCapturedVerbatim%27%2C%20%27captureHashesVerified%27%2C%20%27allConversationObligationsMapped%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-CONVERSATION-CRITICAL-DELIVERY%27%2C%20%27critical%20classification%20of%20all%20conversation%20and%20inherited%20obligations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20conversation%20requirement%20and%20every%20inherited%20ledger%20obligation%20is%20critical%20and%20blocks%20a%20full-scope%20delivery%20or%20release-completion%20claim%20while%20it%20lacks%20required%20exact-commit%20evidence.%20Existing%20source%2C%20scope%2C%20assertions%2C%20fixtures%2C%20runtimes%20and%20checkpoint%20execution%20order%20remain%20intact.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27allRequirementsCritical%27%2C%20%27unverifiedRowsBlockFullScopeDelivery%27%2C%20%27inheritedScopeAndCheckpointsPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27associativeFoundationRequest%27%2C%20stackSource%2C%20%27associative-stack-and-theoretical-foundation%27%2C%20%27associative-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-STACK-PINNED-SOURCE-AUDIT%27%2C%20%27pinned%20audit%20of%20the%20referenced%20associative%20technology%20stack%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20project%20audit%20reads%20the%20referenced%20formal-ai%20associative%20technology%20stack%20at%20a%20recorded%20immutable%20revision%20and%20records%20its%20content%20hash%2C%20providers%20and%20dependency-role%20boundaries.%20A%20moving%20main%20URL%20or%20a%20provider%20name%20alone%20does%20not%20establish%20adoption.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27associativeStackSourceReadAndPinned%27%2C%20%27stackContentHashRecorded%27%2C%20%27providerRolesClassified%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-STACK-PROJECT-WIDE-USE%27%2C%20%27associative%20stack%20adoption%20across%20the%20entire%20project%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27An%20executable%20project-wide%20audit%20covers%20both%20packages%2C%20code%2C%20grammars%2C%20translation%2C%20tools%2C%20documentation%20and%20dependencies%20against%20the%20relevant%20associative%20stack%20obligations.%20Direct%20runtime%20providers%2C%20compatibility%20or%20theoretical%20alignment%20and%20development%20tools%20are%20distinguished%3B%20unrelated%20formal-ai%20dependencies%20are%20not%20blindly%20introduced.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27entireProjectStackUsageAudited%27%2C%20%27actualCodeAndDependenciesTraced%27%2C%20%27runtimeCompatibilityAndDevelopmentRolesDistinct%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-THEORY-FOUNDATION-PINNED-SOURCE-AUDIT%27%2C%20%27pinned%20philosophical%20and%20theoretical%20meta-theory%20foundation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20meta-theory%20source%20is%20read%20at%20an%20immutable%20revision%20with%20archived%20releases%20and%20drafts%20identified%20separately.%20Adopted%20definitions%2C%20assumptions%20and%20provenance%20are%20recorded%20explicitly%3B%20a%20repository%20citation%20alone%20is%20insufficient%20as%20a%20theoretical%20foundation.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27metaTheorySourceReadAndPinned%27%2C%20%27archivesAndDraftsDistinguished%27%2C%20%27adoptedDefinitionsAndAssumptionsTraced%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27associativeFoundationRequest%27%2C%20stackSource%2C%20%27associative-stack-and-theoretical-foundation%27%2C%20%27associative-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-THEORY-FOUNDATION-PROJECT-WIDE-APPLICATION%27%2C%20%27meta-theory%20foundation%20applied%20to%20the%20common%20links%20model%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20common%20concept%2C%20grammar%2C%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%2C%20entity%20and%20relationship%20representation%20applies%20the%20adopted%20links%20meta-theory%20definitions%20throughout%20both%20packages.%20Model%20choices%2C%20theoretical%20premises%20and%20operational%20encodings%20remain%20explicit%20inspectable%20links%20with%20source%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27metaTheoryDefinitionsAppliedProjectWide%27%2C%20%27modelPremisesAreInspectableLinks%27%2C%20%27operationalEncodingsRetainProvenance%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-THEORY-FOUNDATION-CONSUMER-BOUNDARIES%27%2C%20%27theoretical%20foundation%20separated%20from%20consumer%20proof%20authority%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20shared%20philosophical%20and%20theoretical%20links%20foundation%20does%20not%20silently%20choose%20a%20universal%20proof%20logic%2C%20Type%3AType%20axiom%20or%20consumer%20execution%20policy.%20Consumer-owned%20logical%20semantics%20and%20proof%20authority%20remain%20separate%20explicit%20model%20choices%20with%20checked%20correspondences.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27theoreticalAndConsumerFoundationsDistinct%27%2C%20%27noSilentUniversalLogicOrSelfTyping%27%2C%20%27consumerProofAuthorityPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27globalConceptSpace%27%2C%20originalSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27workflow-contract%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-FAST-CONTINUOUS-PROGRESS%27%2C%20%27fast%20continuous%20implementation%20between%20bulk%20feedback%20cycles%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Deliver%20the%20complete%20authorized%20scope%20as%20quickly%20as%20available%20resources%20and%20correct%20verification%20permit%2C%20using%20useful%20parallel%20work%20and%20coherent%20batches.%20Continue%20independent%20drafting%20and%20implementation%20while%20CI%20runs%20instead%20of%20waiting%20idle%3B%20speed%20never%20substitutes%20for%20required%20behavior%20or%20evidence.%27%2C%20%5B%27independentWorkContinuesDuringCi%27%2C%20%27deliveryLatencyMinimizedWithoutScopeReduction%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-LATEST-REPOSITORY%27%2C%20%27latest%20repository%20version%20in%20the%20shared%20local%20checkout%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Before%20drafting%20the%20batch%2C%20the%20coordinator%20obtains%20the%20latest%20authorized%20repository%20and%20pull-request%20refs%2C%20reconciles%20required%20main%20changes%20and%20records%20the%20checkout%20revision%20used%20for%20implementation%20and%20CI%20feedback.%27%2C%20%5B%27latestAuthorizedRefsObtained%27%2C%20%27checkoutRevisionRecorded%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-BULK-EXACT-SCOPE%27%2C%20%27one%20bulk%20draft%20of%20exactly%20all%20issue%2C%20pull-request%20and%20conversation%20obligations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Bulk%20work%20covers%20every%20registered%20issue%2C%20pull-request%20and%20conversation%20obligation%2C%20preserving%20all%20inherited%20scope.%20Drafting%2C%20implementation%20and%20reporting%20do%20not%20substitute%20narrower%20capabilities%20or%20omit%20unresolved%20requirements.%27%2C%20%5B%27entireRegisteredScopeIncluded%27%2C%20%27noScopeSubstitutionOrOmission%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-MINIMAL-LOCAL-RESOURCES%27%2C%20%27minimal%20local%20resources%20and%20targeted%20JavaScript%20validation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Local%20work%20uses%20the%20minimum%20resources%20needed%20for%20targeted%20JavaScript%20validation%20and%20authoring.%20Full%20suites%2C%20whole-registry%20experiments%2C%20downstream%20workload%20clones%20and%20native%20toolchain%20matrices%20remain%20CI%20work.%27%2C%20%5B%27targetedJavaScriptOnlyLocally%27%2C%20%27expensiveChecksDelegatedToCI%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-PARALLEL-DELEGATION%27%2C%20%27maximum%20useful%20independent%20agent%20delegation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Independent%20bulk%20tasks%20are%20split%20among%20as%20many%20useful%20authorized%20agents%20as%20the%20available%20concurrency%20permits%2C%20with%20clear%20ownership%20and%20integration%20coordination%20over%20the%20shared%20checkout.%27%2C%20%5B%27independentTasksDelegated%27%2C%20%27availableConcurrencyUsedWithOwnership%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-CONTRIBUTOR-COMMITS%27%2C%20%27every%20contributor%20commits%20its%20reviewable%20work%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20contributor%20with%20implementation%20work%20commits%20its%20explicit%20owned%20paths%2C%20preserving%20other%20agents%20staged%20changes%20and%20retaining%20reviewable%20commit%20provenance%20for%20the%20bulk%20batch.%27%2C%20%5B%27everyContributorWorkCommitted%27%2C%20%27ownedPathsAndCommitProvenanceRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-SINGLE-PUSH-COORDINATOR%27%2C%20%27one%20coordinator%20performs%20batch%20pushes%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Exactly%20one%20authorized%20coordinator%20pushes%20the%20integrated%20batch%20after%20reviewing%20all%20committed%20work.%20Other%20contributors%20commit%20their%20changes%20without%20pushing.%27%2C%20%5B%27singlePushCoordinatorEnforced%27%2C%20%27integratedBatchReviewedBeforePush%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-PREVIOUS-CI-TERMINAL%27%2C%20%27previous%20CI%20fully%20finished%20before%20a%20new%20batch%20push%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Before%20pushing%20the%20next%20integrated%20batch%2C%20the%20coordinator%20verifies%20the%20prior%20relevant%20CI%2FCD%20runs%20are%20fully%20finished%20and%20inspects%20their%20complete%20failure%20feedback.%20The%20batch%20has%20new%20concrete%20requirements%20or%20fi